# scripts/opcount: `toolbench bench parse N` parses N tool calls a model
# wrote (eight find calls, each a query of text, limit and two tags) with
# the generated toolsllm.Parse into the hub's Request (wf10 L7); the cost
# of one call is the slope between the two sizes. The control is hand Go:
# a switch on the tool's name and encoding/json's Unmarshal into the typed
# request. The floor is one pass over the argument text into the typed
# request, the strings sliced from the text.
unit call
sizes 100000 600000
args bench parse {n}
control benchmarks/llmtools/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/llmtools/testdata/floor
